    basic: 'Prioritize the marriage. A single Trump Marriage (40 pts) is worth more than a natural Ace and 3 combined (21 pts). If you have a King and Knight, save them until you need to snatch the lead.',
    intermediate: "The Lead Management: Don't lead your high point cards (Aces/3s) unless you are sure they won't be trumped. Use small cards (2s/4s) to 'bait' out your opponent's high cards before playing your Mariaccio.",
    advanced: 'Defensive Holding: If your opponent has a high score and is close to 250, try to empty their trump reserves early. Without trumps, their marriages in other suits can still be trumped by you, nullifying their bonus point potential.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Memory: You MUST track the remaining points in the deck as you approach 250. If there are no Aces/3s left, it's very hard to catch up without a marriage.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Call Out: Be bold with the 250-point call. If you are at 240 and you take a King (4 pts) of trumps, you are at 244 plus potentially secret marriages.',
      },
